The Afghans paid the price for the obscuration of these peasants, which were completely dominated by Al-Ká'ida, but their situation has not been improved by our time.
Former mujaweeks, an Afghan government and the current Taliban coincide in an effort to preserve women in a subordinate position.
Major dignitaries from the war against Soviet troops returned to power in 2001.
