Under the pressure of competition at both the international and domestic European level, the government of the Czech Republic will be forced to continue to look for ways to further reduce the social level of the population.
Therefore, this trend is system-specific.
The solution is targeted politico-social reforms, which will strengthen the capital participation of the state in the economy, strengthen the influence of citizens on the government and weaken the monopoly position of private capital in society in favor of the state.
