Argo: When It's Worst the Worst, Call Hollywood
In November 1979, a mob of demonstrating Islamist students seized an U.S. embassies in Tehran and seized 52 diplomats hostage.
They should have been released in extensiated shahah of Mohamz Réza Páhlavi, who after the revolution fled to the United States, who were the patroness of his regime for several decades.
For the U.S. administration, the Situation did not offer a positive starting point-raising shair overboard, because it would fundamentally jeopardize trust in allies in other countries.
The release of the hostages, however, in Iran, where the revolution resulted in the establishment of a theocratic regime, she was unable to achieve.
It was a brink for the prestige of the United States, which was later exaggerated by the fiassin of an attempt to liberate the hostage by force.
Imprisoned diplomats were eventually dismissed after 444 days after the negotiations were brokered by the Algerian government.
At home, their dread provoked a wave of self-reliance and anti-Iranian sentiment.
The debacle in Iran contributed significantly to Jimmy Carter's loss with Ronald Reagan in the 1980 presidential election.
Directed by actor Ben Affleck Argo describes an episode of the history that gave America a small victorious victory.
Just before occupy the embassy, six employees fled it.
After difficult peripetition, they ended up in the residence of the Canadian ambassador.
The CIA, in cooperation with the Canadian authorities, managed to get them out of Iran, helping an extravagant covering story - they went to Canadian passports as members of a film crew that inspected locations for filming a sci-fi movie in the country.
Commitment of Genuine Genres
Tony Mendez, an "exfiltration" expert on "exfiltration", also required Hollywood's cooperation.
In order to be plausible the legend, the film project was written in specialized magazines, there were press conferences, a fictitious production company had a real office.
The details of the operation have been concealed for a long time, the film is based on Tony Mendez's memoir.
Affleck's film is a peculiar combination of multiple genres.
On the one hand a realistically conceived political thriller, at the same time the so-called "caper movie", the story of a successful piece, a double-destepair - an example is a series of Danny's partners.
The film alternates moods - on the one hand the documentary sequences from Tehran (in the subsidy sequence there are iconic historical photographs of the events and the way in which the same situations have been demonstrated in the film - there are no big differences in this).
On the other hand, lightweight passages from Hollywood, dealt with ironic and mild exaggeration.
And then the scenes from the headquarters of the CIA and other institutions -men in suits discuss the situation at the negotiating tables, in the hallways of the office, on the phone...
Ben Affleck managed to reboot his career in a remarkable way.
The mocking an actor became a respected director, and even his acting ceased to be the target of ironic remarks.
Argo is his third full-yelding film after Gone Baby Gone (2007) and thriller City (2010).
At the same time, it's Affleck's first film that doesn't take place in the director's home Boston.
Feeling for the atmosphere of the place was one of the characteristics that the director's older films elevated above the Hollywood standard.
And Affleck manifests him in Argo, where Tehran "plays" Canada.
The finest scenes in the film take place on the streets, while reconstructing real events - the introductory sequence of the fall of the embossed is immersive in its clarification, which at the same time conveys the emotion of confusion and unconvincibility, which arises when history is suddenly moved.
Affleck and his collaborators achieve a similar effect in fictional (false crew at the Tehran bazaar).
Too many events in too many places
The director also had to cope with the fact that the narrated story doesn't actually offer much in the cinematic sense of suspensive scenes.
Quite successfully, he almost cooperates with it, sometimes he thinks something about the reality - everything does not come out so elegantly there (a scene in which the impending crisis at Tehran airport turns the phone call in America and the chase after the runway looks quite far-fruited.).
But Arga's weakness is the distraction resulting from the need to show too many events in too many places.
Alan Arkin and John Goodman are very charaminate in the roles of Hollywood collaborators, but their characters deserve more space and are far from the only ones in the film.
Affleck's film kind of loses a dramatic turn, it's a picture that can be watched with slight interest, to appreciate the realization and retro style evoking thrillers of the 70's.
But it is difficult to deduct.
As a commemoration of one living history in a certain way and a proof of how exaggerated the notions of omnipotent and omniscient secret services are, it will suffice.
Inflating balloon rules, banana and circus
The server www.bankovnipoplaty.com, which annually announces a poll for the most ridiculous bank fee, has now decided to announce a competition for "the most absurd regulations or ideas from the EU workshop".
"We were led to the last event, when the EU plans to adopt a 40 per cent quota for women in the leadership of large European companies," Patrik Nacher, the organizer of the poll, told Právo.
Among the nominated absurdities, for example, there is a recent European court decision to unify insurance premium rates for men and women.
So far, women have been preferential in the prices of life insurance, because they are objectively less risky for insurance companies.
"Other unbelievable EU ideas can be nominated by people until the end of this year.
Voting will then take place until the end of February 2013," Nacher said.
Controversial EU regulations also include mandatory mixing of biofuels into fuels, resulting in a detrimental to nature, while prohibiting the use of reliable mercury thermometries just because they contain a relatively small amount of dangerous substances, or a hen cage-sized directive, due to which eggs have become significantly more expensive this year.
Criticism has previously also faced an effective ban on the use of the term Spread butter or the elimination of classic light bulbs from sale.
High-quality bananas should be 14 centimeters
The EU's apparatus often decides under the pressure of a trade or an industrial or industrial lobby, whose demands in Brussels are usually defended by a state or a group of states (so the Czech Republic is now pushing the demands of its banks with the threat of vet).
For example, bananas of the highest quality had to reach a length of at least 14 centimeters in the Union and were not allowed "anomous curvature".
At the same time, the European Commission has defended itself by harmonising only harmonious national standards complicate trading.
In spite of resistance from some states, the EU has already softened standards on fruit and vegetables, pointing out that existing directives lead to food waste.
Last year's EU regulation may also be a candidate for victories in the poll, according to which for sold inflatable balloons it must be mandatory that children under the age of 8 must not inflaphese unsupervised adults.
The EU has appealed for U.S. research, according to which balloons among the toys are the leading cause of the death of children to suffocum.
A similar restriction now applies to children under the age of 14 when bluishing into go-throwers.
Curiosurance ideas are also born at home
The rule concerning the European officials themselves - anyone who has an official function in the EU cannot use the name Macedonia with regard to the sensibilities of the topic for Greece and must talk about FYROM (Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia).
In cooperation with the Association of Liberal Economists Laissez Faire nominate in a poll, in addition to some above-mentioned absurdities, as well as an EU regulation on the volume of food inventories on the territory of a Member State.
The EU has determined the maximum volumes of food supplies that could be located on the territory of the Czech Republic on the day of our accession to the Union.
The Czech Republic then exceeded, for e.g. the stipulated volumes for canned mushrooms, for which it was threatened with a hefty fine.
Organizers of the poll were also intrigued by the idea of claiming to some countries that they do not have the sea, and the idea of granting subsidies on the application for a subsidy to receive a subsidy.
However, these ideas did not arise in Brussels, but in Prague.
"We are handicapped by the fact that we don't have the sea.
“We will ask the European Union for a refund,” said Jaroslav Palas (ČSSD), Minister of Attorney (ČSSD).
As an arguing, he stated that a lot of grain were born in our country and as a result of the so-called interventional purchases, the state had full warehouses, which he had to export.
The EU should have paid us hundreds of millions of euros, according to Palas.
In the end, the European Commission came out to accommodate the Czech Republic by organizing a tender for the purchase of grain from countries that do not have access to the sea.
The subsidy for obtaining the subsidy was offered to municipalities by the Ministry of Regional Development managed by Minister Pavel Němec (US-DEU), specifically to write an application for a subsidy.
EU: Bizarre regulations are an tribute
While the regulations in the Member States easily become the target of critiques, the EU's efforts to regulate and, at the same time for more efficient functioning and the development of the entire Union, according to a number of experts, it deserves recognition.
According to experts, a more serious problem, according to experts, the use of EU subsidies for projects that do not even have a hint to deepening European integration, but which Member States negotiated during budgetary negotiations.
Emotions among the Czechs also arouse the fact that, just like other EU countries, the Czech Republic in Brussels must fight for the right to a specific designation of its traditional products, while it does not always succeed in this struggle.
After a six-year-long battle with the Germans and the Austrians, the Czechs defended the designation of Olomouc curbs, but domestic rum, the tradition of which dates back to the 19th-centicurse, our producers had to renaming our producers.
The naming of rum can be carried only by products from cane distillate, and not from sugar beets.
In the official list of registered EU products in the society of world-renowned feta and gorgonzola, marzipan from Lübeck, German and Parma ham, for example, Carlsbad biscuits, Pohořelice and Třeboň carp and Žatec hops.
Pardubnice gingerbread and Hořice pine tubes can also take pride in an EU trade mark.
People want me to rescuing the republic, but I'm an aristocrat, says Okamura
Senator, how's he going to think that he wants to run for president?
I don't care about being a senator or a president.
If it works without any problems in our country, I wouldn't run anywhere.
However, I can no longer watch the last twenty-two-year-root the country is stealing as thieves are running here, people are increasing their taxes and retirement.
I didn't have the ambitacy of being a politician.
But when I see something I don't like, I'm trying to come up with a solution to change that.
And since I'm already for forty and I'm an independent non-partisan, I don't have any other way to influence things than running for a senator or president.
You got into the Senate, but you soon went to the castle.
Don’t you turn your back to the people who elected you?
The whole time I said that I will go into the fight for the Castle according to the results in the Senate elections.
I later clarified that if I was elected a senator, I would run for president.
However, my goal is not a function, a function is a tool for how I can realize my visions.
That's why I need the greatest possible influence and the strongest possible mandate.
But the problem is not only the fact that, as a nation we shudder in the pub and in front of the TV, but that we trample on anyone who wants to try to make a change.
This will be accompanied by the media that dishonest a person and which confuse freedom of speech with the freedom to lie.
For example, I was said to bribe journalists or that I was an adviser to Jiří Paroubek.
Let's go to your vision.
You went into the fight for the Castle with a thesis of material and criminal liability of politicians and retrospective property declarations above twenty million.
To do this, you have to change the law.
However, as a president, you do not have such powers, and only the Senate as a whole can propose laws.
How do you want to figure it out?
When, as a citizen, lobbied for a vacuity to be a vacancy, it was possible to enforce it.
The problem is politicking - when someone comes up with a good proposal from the left or from the right, they deliberately denounc themselves, and it delays citizens.
As an independent non-partisan, I have a much greater potential to gain support from all parliamentary parties.
My preference is that without partisan pigeonholing and dogma I can take something that is best for our country, from each side and apply it.
Do you consider yourself a right-wing or left-league?
From the Czech point of view, it seems to me that people put me on the left.
It doesn’t matter to me at all whether a little to the left or a little to the right.
It's important for me to go forward.
I don't care if someone belongs to the left or the right, but I want to unite people.
I will always support any publicly good solution, even if the KSČM or the ODS proposes it, as well as against a bad misdemeanor.
You're going to say you're a populist.
But don't you prove that by what you've said?
When you create a business plan in the company, you also have an ideal goal and vision.
And you're trying to get closer to that.
Someone may call it populism, but all the suggestions I'm talking about already work in the world, or they've been talked about by prominent experts.
But you'll just have passwords without the support of parliament.
You will not be able to do that for a long time in politics.
Or do you think that if you go to people and talk to them, that you will be able to assert criminal and substantive responsibilities, for example?
I don't have an option.
Convincing politicians, journalists and the public and try to get them on our side in order to enforce it.
If I were elected president, it is not a problem to hold a televised live broadcast, where I will ask the leaders of the parliamentary parties to legislate the substantive and criminal liability for politicians, officials, judges and prosecutors.
And maybe they'd have to know why they don't want it.
If there is a strong personality who will narculate misbehaviors, one can pressure the political scene.
Take the direct election of the president, that was due to public pressure.
Honestly, I'm an amateur, that I'm neither a genius nor an intellectual.
For my opinions and visions I try to find allies.
I've only just started in politics and I'm going to try to gain majority support for my program.
I'm trying to move things on my own if it doesn't work, in six years I'm going to finish and I'm going back to the private sector.
It kind of sounds like Okamura should save the Czech Republic.
I'm no s Savior.
I don’t know I won’t do anything in one person, that’s why I’ve been bypassing a number of well-known people if they wouldn’t run for the Senate.
I went after Radim Jančura, he refused because of the amount of work.
So at least I supported investigative journalist Jana Lorenc, who unravelled scavengers with light heating oils.
I've been a candidate saying that people were really dissatisfied, but now I'm in balance.
Sixty percent of people didn't go to the polls, and those who went mostly elected representatives of the establishment.
There are only two independents in the senate.
People have elected the Senate in such a way that it will be difficult to enforce the changes.
Nevertheless, I will fight for my visions, such as the direct election of mayors or governors.
Are you thinking of starting your own party?
I haven't thought about that yet, because I don't have the time to verify every potential sting, and I don't even have the money.
I don't even have money for a presidential campaign, there's only 20 grand in my transparent account.
Don’t you have the money?
You're talking about property returns, what's yours?
I'm going to spend about $60 a.m.
In Prague I have a plot of land for about 25 million, an apartment for tens of millions, another apartment for eight million, a collection of works of art for about ten million, Aston Martin for 3.5 million and Skoda Superb worth a million, and then I have a few millions in my account.
By the way, Aston Martin I have because it was my boyish dream - I've always liked James Bond, who rode in the car, was gallant towards the women and at the same time he struggled against the wrongs and misbehaviors.
You're riding Aston Martin, you've got $60 million property, and you don't have money for a campaign?
You say you want to change the republic, but you don't really want to put your own money into it.
That's not very persuasive.
I don't have $15 million to campaign.
Should I indebted?
I rammed $2.5 million.
The fact that I don't have any sponsors testifies to the fact that my program probably isn't so interested.
And I don't have an obligation on the campaign.
The cost of the campaign will basically cover me with what senator's salaries I'm going to receive.
But I wouldn’t have grown out of it, for example, I wouldn’t be able to pay my son an English school that costs $30 thousand a month.
If I just wanted to make money, I wouldn't run anywhere.
So you'll keep doing business so you can live?
Didn't you say you'd dampen these activities?
But this has nothing to do with salary.
As I promised, I partially subdued my activities.
For example, my representative will become the managing director of a travel agency in the spring.
People would want me to be a Samaritan to rescue the republic.
But I also need to live on something.
How much have you been acquainted to take every month as an entrepreneur?
Twenty-three to $400, which I'm taking on.
And if I'm a president, I'd quit my business.
