It is legally formulated so inaccurately that through this paragraph, state institutions could even control the content of film art and literature.
In comprehensible language, this means nothing but censorship.
After all, no paragraph defines the explicit equality of men and women in writing.
However, another paragraph forbidding the defamation or slandering the Prophet Mohammed and his envoy.
Unclear, however, remains unclear what is defamed and how it will be prosecuted.
Equally dubiously causes the fact that it is forbidden to "interferential people".
